{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f3c0de-9a41-4d7e-9c62-0a1f5d3e77aa",
    "name": "Sunbird RC - Authority & Credential Type Onboarding",
    "description": "Create a new issuing **authority** (a resolvable `did:web`) and a new\n**credential type** (a schema), then prove the type works end to end.\n\nRun folders 0 → 5 in order. Test scripts chain the variables, so nothing\nneeds copying by hand.\n\n### Why a schema is all you create\n\nThe SD-JWT VC Type Metadata at `GET /vct/<slug>` is **generated**, not stored:\n`oid4vci.service.ts getVctTypeMetadata()` finds the published, OID4VCI-enabled\nschema whose slugified `vct` matches the slug and synthesises\n`{ vct, name, display }` from it. Create the schema and the endpoint appears.\n\n### Things that silently break a new type\n\n1. `serviceEndpoint` missing from the DID `services` entry — wallets reject the\n   DID document (`identity.client.ts:31` omits it, so mint DIDs with this\n   collection rather than letting the service auto-provision one).\n2. `vct` given as an absolute URL — `normalizeVct()` passes it through and then\n   nothing serves it. Use a plain display name.\n3. The inner `schema` object must carry **all seven** of `$id`, `$schema`,\n   `description`, `type`, `properties`, `required`, `additionalProperties`\n   (`credential-schema/schema.json`). `description` is the one usually\n   forgotten: it fails with `must have required property 'description'`.\n4. `status` not `PUBLISHED`, or `oid4vciEnabled` not `true` — both are filtered\n   on, so the type never reaches issuer metadata.\n5. `vc+sd-jwt` missing from `oid4vciFormats` — no `/vct/<slug>` document.\n6. Two types sharing a name — identical slugs collide and the first wins.\n7. A `required` property not supplied at offer time — opaque `500 Error issuing\n   credential`; the real ajv reason only appears in the credentials-service log.\n8. `did:rcw` authors cannot be verified by wallets (`unsupportedDidMethod`).\n   Only `did:web` works.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base",
      "value": "https://98.70.36.106.sslip.io"
